T-001 quality-gate cycle-2 remediation — RED/GREEN evidence for the
ECMA-262 `pattern` `$` semantics fix (Critical finding 1) in
plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/validate-facet-manifest.py.

Claim under test: Python's bare `$` in `re.search` matches immediately
before a trailing "\n" as well as at the absolute end of string, so a
value like "sha256:<64hex>\n" wrongly satisfies
`^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$` (and similarly `^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$` for
resolver.version). Draft-07 `pattern` follows ECMA-262 semantics, where
non-multiline `$` asserts end-of-string only — the trailing-newline value
must be REJECTED. Non-vacuity is demonstrated below: the same two fixtures
are wrongly ACCEPTED before the fix (RED) and correctly REJECTED after the
fix (GREEN).

Method: the working-tree copy of validate-facet-manifest.py was temporarily
reverted to its committed HEAD content (`git show HEAD:<path> > <path>`,
byte-identical restore, no `git checkout`/`restore` used per this repo's
guard constraints) to run the pre-fix RED observation, then the fix patch
(saved separately) was re-applied for the GREEN observation. No other file
was touched during this procedure.

================================================================================
RED — pre-fix (validator at committed HEAD content, `re.search` with bare `$`)
================================================================================

Timestamp: 2026-08-17T01:26:45Z

$ python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/validate-facet-manifest.py --manifest tests/fixtures/facet-manifest/schema/context-binding-registry-digest-trailing-newline.json
(no output)
exit=0

$ python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/validate-facet-manifest.py --manifest tests/fixtures/facet-manifest/schema/resolver-version-trailing-newline.json
(no output)
exit=0

Observation: both fixtures — whose `context_binding.registry_digest` /
`resolver.version` values carry a real trailing "\n" that should NOT match
the ECMA-262 non-multiline `$` anchor — are WRONGLY ACCEPTED (exit 0, no
diagnostics). This confirms the bug is real and the new fixtures are
non-vacuous (they fail against the unfixed validator).

================================================================================
GREEN — post-fix (validator with `_ecma_anchor` / `_compile_pattern`, `\Z`)
================================================================================

Timestamp: 2026-08-17T01:27:09Z

$ python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/validate-facet-manifest.py --manifest tests/fixtures/facet-manifest/schema/context-binding-registry-digest-trailing-newline.json
facet-manifest: schema-invalid: /context_binding/registry_digest: does not match pattern '^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$'
exit=1

$ python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/validate-facet-manifest.py --manifest tests/fixtures/facet-manifest/schema/resolver-version-trailing-newline.json
facet-manifest: schema-invalid: /resolver/version: does not match pattern '^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$'
exit=1

Sanity check — valid-base.json (no trailing newline anywhere) still passes
after the fix, confirming the `\Z` rewrite did not over-tighten normal
(non-trailing-newline) instances:

$ python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/validate-facet-manifest.py --manifest tests/fixtures/facet-manifest/schema/valid-base.json
(no output)
exit=0

================================================================================
Conclusion
================================================================================

Both new fixtures are non-vacuous: they wrongly PASS (RED, exit 0) against
the pre-fix validator and correctly FAIL with a `schema-invalid` diagnostic
pinning the exact offending JSON Pointer (GREEN, exit 1) against the
post-fix validator. The fix (`_ecma_anchor` rewriting unescaped,
non-character-class `$` to `\Z` before `re.compile`) is proven to close the
gap described in evaluator finding 1 without breaking the unrelated
trailing-newline-free baseline fixture.
